Well, I'd like to point out to the first extropian squirrel that although
I plan to do something more in depth on the environment thing shortly,
for now I'd simply like to point out that I agree with his point about
advanced tech and wish that the US government had agreed too during the
Exxon Valdez cleanup; rather than go with heavy use of bioremediation,
it was tested only along a couple-hundred-foot length of coast; the
official mandated method mainly used in the cleanup was ye olde victorian
